  "starterCode": "import math\ndef solve(X, y, W1, b1, W2, b2, lr=0.01):\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, mathematically sound implementation.\n\n### ⚡ Implementation\n```python\nimport math\ndef solve(X, y, W1, b1, W2, b2, lr=0.01):\n    # One full-batch gradient step for a 2-layer sigmoid MLP, binary labels.\n    def sig(z): return 1/(1+math.exp(-max(-60,min(60,z))))\n    n=len(X); h=len(W1[0]); d=len(X[0])\n    Z=[]; A=[]; P=[]\n    for row in X:\n      z=[b1[j]+sum(row[k]*W1[k][j] for k in range(d)) for j in range(h)]\n      a=[sig(v) for v in z]; p=sig(b2[0]+sum(a[j]*W2[j][0] for j in range(h)))\n      Z.append(z); A.append(a); P.append(p)\n    dz2=[(P[i]-y[i])/n for i in range(n)]\n    gW2=[[sum(A[i][j]*dz2[i] for i in range(n))] for j in range(h)]\n    gb2=sum(dz2)\n    dz1=[[dz2[i]*W2[j][0]*A[i][j]*(1-A[i][j]) for j in range(h)] for i in range(n)]\n    gW1=[[sum(X[i][k]*dz1[i][j] for i in range(n)) for j in range(h)] for k in range(d)]\n    gb1=[sum(dz1[i][j] for i in range(n)) for j in range(h)]\n    W1n=[[W1[k][j]-lr*gW1[k][j] for j in range(h)] for k in range(d)]\n    b1n=[b1[j]-lr*gb1[j] for j in range(h)]\n    W2n=[[W2[j][0]-lr*gW2[j][0]] for j in range(h)]\n    b2n=[b2[0]-lr*gb2]\n    return W1n,b1n,W2n,b2n\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$",
